If `optimizeExplicitEnvironmentDeps()` throws an exception, `initState` will remain stuck at `'initializing'` and subsequent calls to `init()` will return early without retrying. This means initialization can never be retried after a failure.

```typescript
async function init() {
  if (depsOptimizer.initState !== 'idle') return
  depsOptimizer.initState = 'initializing'

  try {
    depsOptimizer.metadata = await optimizeExplicitEnvironmentDeps(environment)
    depsOptimizer.initState = 'initialized'
  } catch (error) {
    depsOptimizer.initState = 'idle'
    throw error
  }
}
```
